#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:1
msgid "Binary Installation on Ubuntu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:3
msgid ""
"Jetty binaries are provided for Ubuntu Noble (24.04). The Jetty binaries are "
"hosted in the packages.osrfoundation.org repository. To install all of them, "
"the metapackage `gz-jetty` can be installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:7
msgid "First install some necessary tools:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:9
msgid ""
"sudo apt-get update\n"
"sudo apt-get install curl lsb-release gnupg\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:14
msgid "Then install Gazebo Jetty:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:17
msgid ""
"sudo curl https://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo.gpg --output /usr/share/"
"keyrings/pkgs-osrf-archive-keyring.gpg\n"
"echo \"deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/"
"pkgs-osrf-archive-keyring.gpg] https://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo/"
"ubuntu-stable $(lsb_release -cs) main\" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/"
"gazebo-stable.list > /dev/null\n"
"sudo apt-get update\n"
"sudo apt-get install gz-jetty\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:24
msgid ""
"All libraries should be ready to use and the `gz sim` app ready to be "
"executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:26
msgid ""
"Head back to the [Getting started](getstarted) page to start using Gazebo!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:30
msgid "Server-only installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:32
msgid ""
"For headless and CI environments where the GUI is not needed, the `gz-sim10-"
"server` package provides a lightweight alternative. It installs only the "
"Gazebo simulation server (`gz-sim-server`) without any GUI or Qt "
"dependencies, resulting in a significantly smaller installation footprint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:37
msgid ""
"After configuring the repository (same as above), install the server-only "
"package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:40
msgid "sudo apt-get install gz-sim10-server\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:44
msgid ""
"The server-only package includes the DART physics engine and the core "
"simulation server plugins. To start a headless simulation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:47
msgid "/usr/libexec/gz/sim10/gz-sim-server <world_file.sdf>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:52
msgid ""
"The server-only binary is installed at `/usr/libexec/gz/sim10/gz-sim-"
"server`, which is not in the `PATH` by default. The regular `gz sim -s` "
"command is not available in the server-only installation since it requires "
"the full `gz-sim10-cli` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:58
msgid "Uninstalling binary install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:60
msgid ""
"If you need to uninstall Gazebo or switch to a source-based install once you "
"have already installed the library from binaries, run the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu.md:63
msgid "sudo apt remove gz-jetty && sudo apt autoremove\n"
msgstr ""

